\fBtags\fP \-\- A dictionary of strings can be passed as tag metadata to the network interface object.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnetwork_security_group\fP \-\- The name of the existing network security group to assign to the network interface.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBvirtual_machine\fP \-\- The name of the existing virtual machine to assign to the network interface.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdns_settings\fP \-\- 
.sp
An optional dictionary representing a valid NetworkInterfaceDnsSettings object. Valid parameters are:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdns_servers\fP: List of DNS server IP addresses. Use \(aqAzureProvidedDNS\(aq to switch to Azure provided DNS
resolution. \(aqAzureProvidedDNS\(aq value cannot be combined with other IPs, it must be the only value in
dns_servers collection.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinternal_dns_name_label\fP: Relative DNS name for this NIC used for internal communications between VMs in
the same virtual network.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinternal_fqdn\fP: Fully qualified DNS name supporting internal communications between VMs in the same virtual
network.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinternal_domain_name_suffix\fP: Even if internal_dns_name_label is not specified, a DNS entry is created for
the primary NIC of the VM. This DNS name can be constructed by concatenating the VM name with the value of
